Description: r7 (SM-N770F) camera orientation and video recording fixes
 Four problems, one of them only partly:
 .
 1) Preview stuck in landscape: rotating landscape->portrait left the preview
    in landscape. On this compositor (phoc) QScreen.orientation is never updated
    - the output is rotated at composition time and the client is not told - so
    Qt's VideoOutput.autoOrientation does not work and applies an orientation
    that is never reset on rotation. Fixed by autoOrientation=false plus driving
    the orientation explicitly from QtSensors OrientationSensor (iio-sensor-proxy
    backend): VideoOutput.orientation = -(compositor transform), i.e.
    code 4 (RightUp, t270)->+90, 3 (LeftUp)->-90, 2 (TopDown)->180, portrait->0.
 .
 2) Photos taken in landscape were saved as portrait. CaptureFilter receives the
    frame before VideoOutput.orientation, which only affects display, so the
    orientation was never baked in. A rotation property was added to
    CaptureFilter; the QImage is rotated by -viewfinder.orientation before saving
    (QTransform rotates clockwise, VideoOutput counter-clockwise, hence negative).
 .
 3) Video recordings came out black: the recording directory is now derived from
    the same MoviesLocation as outputPath, and created (new
    FileManager.createDirectoryAbsolute). The old code created a home-relative
    "/Videos/droidian-camera" while outputPath used MoviesLocation, and since
    XDG_VIDEOS_DIR="$HOME/" the two never matched. filesink then failed, taking
    the whole pipeline down - black preview and an empty recording.
 .
 4) (Partial) Black video thumbnails: ThumbnailGenerator now uses
    QVideoFrame::image() instead of manual bits()+imageFormatFromPixelFormat.
    However, video playback on this device is hardware-decoded (Halium droid
    codec) and the frames are not CPU-accessible, so the play-and-probe approach
    cannot produce a thumbnail at all. KNOWN LIMITATION: video thumbnails stay
    black. The correct fix is a record-time thumbnail taken from the preview
    frame; deferred. Recording and playback themselves work fully.
Author: Yunus Tan <yunus.tan@outlook.com.tr>
Origin: downstream, r7 (SM-N770F) Droidian port
